POST-RUN CORRECTION (same session, the verify-first loop catching its author AGAIN): the
conjectured threshold "B <= 13 => bounded diameter" is FALSE -- the DFS itself found the
symmetric three-piece family {0,1} u {c-1,c,c+1} u {2c-1,2c} (a rank-2 GAP) with B = 13 at every
diameter (gcd 1). The TRUE stability threshold is B <= 12 => D <= 7 (exhaustive D <= 60: max
D at B <= 12 is 7), SHARP: b = 1 is the last stable excess for restricted sums at k = 7.
The B = 13 escapers are rank-2 GAPs = exactly opus-S181's loose/dissociated family: the burden
levels {11 = AP, 12 = AP-with-hole, 13 = rank-2 GAP, >= 14 = spread} mirror the LRC branch tree.
